 "summaries": [
  {
   "section": "Exterior",
   "text": "There are minor misc scratches around the vehicle. Normal for mileage and most too small to see in photos. PDR on doors and fenders. Dent 1-2 on both right doors. Rear bumper has been repainted. The paint shows some wear and tear that is consistent with age and mileage. Paint chips on hood. The underside shows areas of surface rust. See pictures. Damage 12” on both front and rear bumpers. Rear bumper has been repainted. The windshield has miscellaneous stone chips. Sun shade missing from sun roof. Both front tires and the driver side rear tire show 6/32 tread remaining. Passenger side rear tire shows 7/32 tread remaining. The passenger side front wheel and both rear wheels show curb rash."
  },
  {
   "section": "Interior",
   "text": "Seats show signs of heavy usage. Right front seat is damaged. Wear and tear heavily visible. See pictures. The inner door panels show wear consistent with age and mileage. Driver door arm rest worn, split. Right front door handle is peeling. The interior trim shows normal wear consistent with age and mileage. The heater system is not blowing as hot as it should. This may be a sign that the thermostat has failed or is starting to fail. There are other more serious issues that could cause this as well. More diagnosis is necessary. Sun shade missing. Headliner is dirty needs cleaning. The A/C is not blowing cold and the compressor did not turn on. The A/C system is not functioning. Further diagnosis is necessary. The blower motor does not work. Right sun visor latch broken. Power windows, door locks and mirrors operate as they should at the time of the inspection."
  },
  {
   "section": "Mechanical",
   "text": "The accessible under hood fluids were noted to be at acceptable levels. There were no leaks noted. The belts and hoses were noted to be in good condition."
  },
  {
   "section": "Road Test",
   "text": "The engine starts, runs and idles. The Rpm's randomly get stuck around 2-3 rpm. Requires further diagnosis. The vehicle accelerates, the transmission operates smoothly and the brakes stop the vehicle effectively. The steering is responsive and the suspension firm. The left front axle makes noise, outer CV boot split open. A scan of the vehicles on board diagnostic system found multiple codes, none power train related. See pictures."
  }
 ],
